Subject: [PATCH] meson: Tau probes through the libc layer, as Embox

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1633,11 +1633,11 @@
   'sysconf': '#include <unistd.h>',
 }
 
-# Embox: without a prefix, has_function declares the function itself and finds
+# Embox and Tau: without a prefix, has_function declares the function itself and finds
 # whatever symbol the kernel's own libc has. Mesa is compiled against the libc
 # layer on top of it (sprt), so ask through its headers. qsort_s there is the
 # Microsoft one (context first), which util_qsort_r would call as C11's.
-if host_machine.system() == 'embox'
+if host_machine.system() in ['embox', 'tau']
   functions_to_detect = {
     'strtof': '#include <stdlib.h>',
     'mkostemp': '#include <stdlib.h>',
